The Programming Life Cycle is a structured process used to develop software. It helps ensure that the SkillsTrack Learner Support Portal is carefully planned, designed, tested and improved before final deployment. The six main stages are Analysis, Design, Coding, Testing, Implementation and Review.Leaner Uses Cases

(1) The 6 Stages 

1.1 Analysis: during this phase, the problem is studied and requirements are gathered. 

Activities: 
Understand the client brief 
Identify users 
Identify system requirements 
Define project scope 
Create user stories 
Create acceptance criteria 

Output: 
Problem statement 
Requirements document 

2.1 Design: during this phase, the solution is planned before coding begins. 

Activities: 
Design Firebase structure 
Create flowcharts 
Write pseudocode 
Plan classes and objects 
Design page layout 

Output: 
Data model 
Flowcharts 
Wireframes 

3.1 Coding: during this phase, the application is developed using JavaScript, HTML and CSS. 

Activities: 
Build interface 
Create forms 
Write JavaScript functions 
Create task manager 
Implement user interactions 

Output: 
Working application prototype 

 

4.1 Testing: during this phase, bugs and errors are identified. 

Activities: 
Test login form 
Test calculations 
Test validation 
Check JavaScript console 
Fix errors 

Output: 
Corrected and working code 

5.1 Implementation: During this phase, the system becomes available for users. 

Activities: 
Deploy working version 
Connect Firebase 
Allow users to interact with features 

Output: 
Functional Learner Support Portal 

6.1 Review and Maintenance: during this phase, feedback is collected and improvements are made. 

Activities: 
Receive assessor feedback 
Review code quality 
Improve user experience 
Fix remaining issues 

Output: 
Improved final version 

(7) Uses Cases

1.Account Registration > sing up, verify email and create a profile.
2.Access Resources > download study materials, guides and multimedia.
3.Progress Tracking > view dashboard showing completed modules, scores and achievement.
4.Mentorship Requests > booking a one-on-one sessions with facilitator.
5.Discussion Participation > join forums, ask questions and collaborate with peers.
6.Support Ticket Submission > Report issues or request for help from admins.

7.2 Facilitator Uses Cases

1.Session Scheduling > set availability and mange leaner booking.
2.Resource Contribution . upload guides, tutorials or recorded lectures.
3.Leaner Feedback > provide comments, grade or improvement suggestion.
4.Communication >  chart, video call, or respond to learner questions.

7.3 Admin Uses Cases

1.User Management > approve accounts, assign roles and deactivate inactive users.
2.Content Moderation > review forum posts, flag inappropriate concent.
3.System Monitoring > track uptime, performance and error logs.
4.Analytics Reporting > generate report on leaner engagement and success rates.
5.Security Oversight > manage permissions, encryption and compliance.